SUMMARY:Wonder Zone Grand Opening Weekend!
DESCRIPTION:Join Lancaster Science Factory to celebrate the Grand Opening Weekend of the Wonder Zone! The Wonder Zone is a brand new exhibit area designed for kids ages 3-5\, but accessible and enjoyable for all ages! This exhibit are was made possible by a generous lead donation from the Dart Foundation. Thank you! \nWonder Zone Weekend Timeline:\nSaturday\, November 14th \n9:00am-10:00am        Members ONLY Morning. \n\nLancaster Science Factory members are invited to experience the Wonder Zone early! Please RSVP to this event through the linked Eventbrite. This event is free for members\, just be sure to bring your membership card!\n\n10:00am-1:00pm       Lancaster Libraries\, Intermediate Unit 13\, and Lancaster Rec Activities \n\n Join us to explore the Wonder Zone! To help us celebrate\, our friends from Lancaster Libraries will have the Bookmobile on site and do hourly story times in the Castagna Learning Center. \nLancaster Rec and Intermediate Unit 13 will have hands-on STEM and literacy-based activities on the exhibit floor.   \n\nSunday\, November 15th \n1:00 and 3:00             Starry Night Slime Lab \n\nContinue the Wonder Zone celebrations on Sunday with Starry Night Slime Lab! Join us for a 30-minute guided hands-on workshop where participants will create their own slime. Learn how a few simple ingredients come together to make this stretchy- squishy favorite! Workshops will take place twice each scheduled day\, so choose the time that works best for you!\nThis slime lab is specially themed to match our new Reach exhibit and donor wall in the Wonder Zone\, so be sure to check it out while you are here!\n\nAbout the Wonder Zone:\nJoin us for the grand opening of the Wonder Zone\, 12 exhibit experiences themed around light\, sound\, forces and motion\, and engineering. This space was designed to be accessible to kids ages 3-5 years old and their families\, but will be enjoyed by all.\n\nSome of the new exhibit experiences include:\n\nEverbright\, an  interactive light wall made of hundreds of dials that change colors when you turn them. Think the Lite-Brite of your childhood\, but with hundreds of analog dials and no removable parts.\nRamps and Magneticars- (see the example) – design your car using the large\, foam magnetic pieces. Design your ramp. Can you make an ice cream truck that goes slow? A race car that goes fast?\nImmersive air exhibit – Step inside the circle and float balls or scarves on a stream of air that you can interact with.\nShape projector – explore light\, color and shadow with the shape projector!
URL:https://lancastersciencefactory.org/event/wonder-zone-grand-opening-weekend/
LOCATION:The Lancaster Science Factory\, 454 New Holland Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lancastersciencefactory.org/wp-content/uploads/Wonder-Zone-Event-Cover-1.png
GEO:40.0461822;-76.2963319
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=The Lancaster Science Factory 454 New Holland Ave Lancaster PA 17602 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=454 New Holland Ave:geo:-76.2963319,40.0461822
END:VEVENT
